  "name": "Notes of an Erythrokeramist (Excerpt)",
  "sourceUrl": "https://honkai-star-rail.fandom.com/wiki/Notes_of_an_Erythrokeramist_(Excerpt)",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-07-11T05:51:38.089Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "label": "Text",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "(...)"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In dreams we dance with families near, yet dawn brings tears for homes no longer here."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In dreams we bid loved ones last goodbye, then wake to find simple joys that make us smile."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Between dreams and waking, life flows on, fragments joined like pearls upon a string."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "We think ourselves wise enough to tell dream from reality —"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But if we never wake, how can we know we dream?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And if we ever dream, how can we call ourselves to wake?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "(...)"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "As stars both rise and set in heaven's dome, all life must bloom then find its final home."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Time flows eternal through worlds vast and deep, while fate weaves webs where all must dance and leap."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "We're but small motes in fate's grand design, brief sparks that in life's vast dome shine."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "We tremble wild as clouds that drift and fade —"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Why seek to grasp what can't be understood? Why build what world has never stood?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Why build on beds already made? Why seek depths beneath the laid?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What senses cannot grasp need not be. If it is, it is as nothing."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "(...)"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In White Dryad's dance I see sweet scents grow, while feast songs taste like honey's gentle flow."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Garden perfumes show rainbow light, while honey streams sing pure delight."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "My soul sees truth in all that lives and grows, while my mind breaks free from reason's rigid throes."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A flower greets me, all senses embrace it, there it dwells —"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yet to record, sketch, or preserve it, into something else it will transform."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "(...)"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
